From 87aff499d9e7d5d34fc1960c11aa566a44ec2c8f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pierre-Yves Le Borgne <pylaterreur@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 14:54:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Run the unit tests in the Linux pip job again.

kokoro/gcp_ubuntu/pip/test_script.sh passed "${TEST_EXCLUDE}" to find,
which expands to the first element of the array only ("-not"). find
then looked for directories named *_test.py, found none, and xargs ran
python3 once without arguments, which exits with 0. So since
e057852 (June 2024) the job has not run any of the tests under tink/,
with or without KMS. Expand the whole array: without -k, find now
returns the 59 test files outside cc/pybind and integration/.

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GwUvhmzgfkiZ6vo4uGyesN
---
 kokoro/gcp_ubuntu/pip/test_script.sh | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/kokoro/gcp_ubuntu/pip/test_script.sh b/kokoro/gcp_ubuntu/pip/test_script.sh
index 116bdc6..001d413 100755
--- a/kokoro/gcp_ubuntu/pip/test_script.sh
+++ b/kokoro/gcp_ubuntu/pip/test_script.sh
@@ -82,7 +82,7 @@ else
   TEST_EXCLUDE+=( -not -path "*integration/*" )
 fi
 readonly TEST_EXCLUDE
-find tink/ "${TEST_EXCLUDE}" -type f -name "*_test.py" -print0 \
+find tink/ "${TEST_EXCLUDE[@]}" -type f -name "*_test.py" -print0 \
   | xargs -0 -n1 python3
 
 # Install requirements for examples.
-- 
